entry.content:
## New: Deathlink and Filler Traps
These options used to be disabled before. You _can_ die in Fantasy Life but it mostly asks if you wanna use a Life Cure on the spot or get revived back at your home, so I figure similarly you can choose to discard a Life Cure (as if you had used it) or teleport back home if you wanna play with deathlink on but would rather not force yourself into losing to an enemy.

As for traps, here are some I came up with, subject to change in the future:
* **Sneak Trap:** replenish your stamina gauge then sneak around in place until it's fully depleted;
* **Run Trap:** replenish your stamina gauge then run around in place until it's fully depleted;
* **Sit Trap:** first drain your entire stamina gauge then sit down until it's fully recovered;
* **Pacifist Trap:** you're not allowed to harm enemies for X time;
* **No Gathering Trap:** you're not allowed to mine, chop, fish or pick up items for X time;
* **No Crafting Trap:** you're not allowed to create items via artisan stations for X time;
* **No Items Trap:** you're not allowed to use consumables for X time;
* **No Shopping Trap:** you're not allowed to purchase anything for X time;
* **Life Change Trap:** you're forced to switch into one of your available lives and be unable to switch them again for X time;
* **Teleport Trap:** you're forced to teleport to one of your available fast travel points and cannot use them again for X time;
* **Famine Trap:** you're forced to consume a food item;
* **Hydration Trap:** you're forced to consume a potion or other drinkable item;

I'm not sure what amount of time can work for the traps that specify something. 1 minute? 5? So I left it open. It is a manual after all.

## New: Bingo Goal
A new goal objective has been added, named Bingo. You can create 3x3, 5x5, 7x7 or 9x9 board of locations logically required as part of the goal. These locations are all named Bingo Board Row A Column B, and their requirements are copied from random existing locations in the APWorld.

Each board tile also has the original location marked as their "entrance" to make it easier to visualize which location you're supposed to do first before you're allowed to check that tile:
<img width="1914" height="641" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/43c1e22d-d4d8-48f7-86e5-1c15215116d9" />

Ideally there should have been some visual aid on the locations and board tiles but for the time being the hinted locations should help. 

Additionally, there are bonus locations for rows, columns and diagonals, which also may only be checked once their corresponding tiles have also been checked out.

## New: Additional Filters for Shops and Chests
* You can now toggle Castele, Port Puerto, Al Maajik or Other shops;
* You can now specify which areas in game to consider for chest locations;

## Changes:
* Not all but several locations have been renamed to be easier to spot at a glance where they're from;
* Some csv files have been removed in favor of readding that info into the respective json files;
* Locations for unlocking bliss bonuses have had their requirements tweaked to require progressive chapters too;
* Temporarily removed locations for finding and equipping item rarities
  * Needs some rework

## Fixes:
* Restricted shop location logic was not respecting the spoiler log

## TODO:
